{
	"version": 5,
	"id": "BsfPLiWJTpZAJ9mCT",
	"notes": "A Weirdboy: an Ork psyker, built on the same Thaumatology: Sorcery chassis as every other psyker in this project (Imperium/Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq), reskinned Ork-flavour and gated by Warp Empowerment exactly as an Astropath or Librarian is, just tuned for raw destructive power over control. The template buys Warp Empowerment 20 (cap 210), the lowest level that covers 'Eadbanger at its full 10 dice (210): the psychic blow that bursts a target's head, built at lore scale rather than party balance. That cap also covers Da Jump (60) and Warpath (18), so this Weirdboy needs no WAAAGH! to cast anything. The WAAAGH! Gestalt bonus (one Empowerment level higher, +10 cap, while in a WAAAGH!, from Ork Physiology below) only matters to a less-developed Weirdboy: at Empowerment 4 (cap 50) Da Jump (60) is castable only inside a WAAAGH!, which is how Weirdboyz cut loose with Da Jump mid-battle.\nPerils of the Warp is unchanged from the human-scale rules (Imperium/ Traits/Psykers and the Warp.adq): Catastrophic failure (fail the Will roll by 10+, or roll an unmodified 18) is, for a Weirdboy specifically, the setting's own trope of an exploding head — Codex background and Black Library both play a Weirdboy's head literally detonating as a routine occupational hazard, not a narrative rarity. Ork society's usual answer is to keep a Painboy or Mek \"attendant\" nearby with tools (a wrench, a shock-lash, sometimes a special hat) to relieve the pressure before it gets that far — flavour for play, not a separate mechanic.\nPoint math: Ork Physiology 311 + psychic package 243 (10 Unusual Background + 20 Psyker Talent 2 + 210 Warp Empowerment 20 + 8 Witch-sight - 5 Social Stigma) + powers 295 modified (210 'Eadbanger x10 + 7 Fists of Gork x2 + 18 Warpath + 60 Da Jump) + skills 15 (Innate Attack (Projectile) 4 included) = 864 points, above framework.md's Senior Agents range because the 'Eadbanger is at lore scale: a rare, dangerous Ork specialist who can pop a head at a glance, a small strategic asset (or liability) in his own right. A \"young,\" less-developed Weirdboy should buy fewer 'Eadbanger levels and the matching lower Empowerment (for example 'Eadbanger x2 at Empowerment 4, cap 50, which is the old 501-point build with Da Jump gated to a WAAAGH!).\n",
	"traits": [
		{
			"id": "TVr94LxXu05mj38ek",
			"name": "Ork Physiology",
			"local_notes": "Lore: An Ork Boy: the baseline greenskin warrior, grown fast, fed on violence, and built to get bigger and meaner the longer it survives. This trait is the shared baseline every growth lens (Nob, Warboss) and every Oddboy specialisation (Mek, Painboy, Weirdboy) builds on top of. Primary sources: Codex: Orks background across editions, Nate Crowley's Ghazghkull Thraka: Prophet of the Waaagh! and Mike Brooks' Brutal Kunnin', calibrated against Dark Heresy/Rogue Trader/Deathwatch/Only War Ork material for relative scale.\n\nDesign: 198 (Attribute Modifiers) + 15 (Basic Move +3) + 10 (Thick Hide) + 10 (High Pain Threshold) + 6 (Hard to Kill 3) + 5 (Rapid Healing) + 6 (Thick Skull) + 15 (Resistant to Disease and Toxins) + 0 (Fungal Physiology) - 10 (Bloodlust) - 10 (Impulsiveness) - 5 (Overconfidence) + 10 (Ork Kunnin' 1) + 5 (WAAAGH! Gestalt) + 6 (Fearlessness 3) + 50 (Injury Tolerance (Damage Reduction), divisor 2) = 311 points of physiology alone, before skills — see the Ork Boy template for a full character, and the growth lenses and Oddboy Talents below for Nobs, Warbosses, Meks, Painboyz and Weirdboyz built on top of it.",
			"tags": [
				"Advantage",
				"Physical",
				"Xenos",
				"Orks"
			],
			"container_type": "ancestry",
			"children": [
				{
					"id": "tYnwz6zQUrzjj4-4C",
					"name": "Attribute Modifiers (Boy)",
					"local_notes": "Design: Framework target: ST 28, DX 11, IQ 8, HT 13, HP 32, SM 0. Increased ST +18 (B14, 10/level, 180) for ST 28 — \"stooped but heavy; brawnier than a man\": Basic Lift 157 lb, far past an unaugmented human and only a shade under an Astartes' ST 30 (strength ladder in framework.md). Increased DX +1 (B15, 20/level, 20) for DX 11 — \"far clumsier than a Marine,\" barely above a Guardsman's own DX 12 despite the far greater ST. Decreased IQ -2 (B16, 20/level, -40) for IQ 8, the framework's own figure for \"not smart, but not helpless either\" — offset in play by Ork Kunnin' below rather than by raw IQ. Increased HT +3 (B15, 10/level, 30) for HT 13. Extra Hit Points +4 (B16, 2/level, 8) for HP 32 (28 base from ST, +4): an Ork soaks up more damage than its ST alone would suggest, matching how much punishment a Boy shrugs off in the fiction. 180+20-40 +30+8 = 198 points.",
					"tags": [
						"Physical"
					],
					"base_points": 198,
					"features": [
						{
							"type": "attribute_bonus",
							"attribute": "st",
							"amount": 18
